      "chapter": "Permutations and Combinations",
      "question": "Everyone in a room shakes hands with everyone else. There are 66 handshakes in all. How many people are in the room?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "\\(10\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "\\(6\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "\\(11\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "\\(12\\)"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "D",
      "step": "Each handshake is a pair of people: \\(n(n-1)/2 = 66\\), so \\(n(n-1) = 132 = 12 \\times 11\\) and \\(n = 12\\).",
      "checked": "n(n−1)/2 = 66 → n² − n − 132 = 0 → (n − 12)(n + 11) = 0 → n = 12. Matches the bank (D)."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-27",
