      "chapter": "Vectors",
      "question": "The vectors \\(\\bar{a} = 2\\hat{i} + \\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k}\\) and \\(\\bar{b} = p\\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}\\) are perpendicular. Then",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "\\(p = -4\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "\\(p = 4\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "\\(p = 2\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "\\(p = -2\\)"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "A",
      "step": "Perpendicular means \\(\\bar{a} \\cdot \\bar{b} = 0\\): \\(2p + 2 + 6 = 0\\), so \\(p = -4\\).",
      "checked": "a·b = 2p + 1·2 + 3·2 = 2p + 8 = 0 → p = −4. Matches the bank (A)."
    },
