      "question": "Which point on this ellipse is the same distance from both its foci? \\[\\dfrac{x^2}{25} + \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1\\]",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "\\((0, 3)\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "\\((5, 0)\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "\\((3, 0)\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "\\((0, 5)\\)"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "A",
      "step": "The foci are \\((\\pm 4, 0)\\), so the point is on the y-axis: \\((0, \\pm 3)\\).",
      "checked": "c² = 25 − 9 = 16 → foci (±4, 0); equidistant → x = 0 → y² = 9 → (0, ±3). (0, 5) is not on the ellipse; (5, 0) and (3, 0) are not equidistant. Matches the bank (A)."
