      "chapter": "Binomial Distribution",
      "question": "In a binomial distribution with \\(n = 18\\), the mean is twice the variance. The probability of success is",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "\\(1\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "step": "Mean \\(np\\) = 2 × variance \\(npq\\), so \\(q = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\) and \\(p = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\).",
      "checked": "np = 2npq → q = 1/2 → p = 1/2 (n = 18 doesn't matter). Matches the bank (B)."
    }
